{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-119034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{3}{x-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the derivative term is already isolated on the left:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{3}{x-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =3\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-119034" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119034" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{(3x-1)^{2}}+C"] ["math" "f(x)=-\\frac{3}{(x-1)^{2}}+C"] ["math" "f(x)=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C"] ["math" "f(x)=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C"] ["math" "f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-1|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119034" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{e}^{2x}=-2x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4{e}^{2x}-2x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}y & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2x}-{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-50136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-2{e}^{2x}-2{x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "y=-2{e}^{2x}-{x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "y=-4{e}^{2x}-2{x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "y=-{e}^{2x}-2{x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "y=-{e}^{2x}-{x}^{2}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-2{e}^{2x}-{x}^{2}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the derivative term is already isolated on the left:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x)=-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "f(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)-6{e}^{-3x}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =1+6{e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+6{e}^{-3x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\text{d}x+6\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x+6(-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3x}) \\\\  & =x-2{e}^{-3x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-119037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x)=2(x+9{e}^{-3x})+C"] ["math" "f(x)=2(x-3{e}^{-3x})+C"] ["math" "f(x)=x+{e}^{-3x}+C"] ["math" "f(x)=x-18{e}^{-3x}+C"] ["math" "f(x)=x-2{e}^{-3x}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=x-2{e}^{-3x}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)+6{x}^{2}=4x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =4x-6{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4x-6{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3}+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}(1-x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x)=2{x}^{2}(1-x)+C"] ["math" "f(x)=2{x}^{2}(3-x)+C"] ["math" "f(x)=2{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-1)+C"] ["math" "f(x)={x}^{2}(2-x)+C"] ["math" "f(x)={x}^{2}(2x-1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=2{x}^{2}(1-x)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-79554" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\sqrt{x}=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-79554" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\sqrt{x}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{2}{3}\\int {x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\frac{2}{5}\\,{x}^{5/2})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-79554" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-79554" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-79554" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{2}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=\\frac{2}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+C{x}^{2}+D"] ["math" "y=\\frac{2}{3}\\,{x}^{3/2}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=\\frac{4}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=\\frac{4}{5}\\,{x}^{3/2}+C{x}^{2}+D"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-79554" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{4}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+Cx+D"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+5=6{x}^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{2}-5.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6{x}^{2}-5)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-5x+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-5x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2{x}^{3}-5x+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})-5(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{2}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=3{x}^{4}-5{x}^{2}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-4{x}^{2}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{4}+Cx+D"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-8\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-8(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =4\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+Cx+D \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-119041" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119041" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C{x}^{2}+D"] ["math" "y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C{x}^{2}+D"] ["math" "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+Cx+D"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119041" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+Cx+D"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=-10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-10\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-10x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-10x+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-10\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D \\\\  & =-5{x}^{2}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-50139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-5{x}^{2}+Cx"] ["math" "y=-5{x}^{2}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=-5{x}^{2}+D"] ["math" "y=5{x}^{2}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=C{x}^{2}+10x+D"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-5{x}^{2}+Cx+D"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation $x\\cdot \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{2}-4x.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6{x}^{2}-4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-4(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+C)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})-2(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-50146" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50146" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y={x}^{4}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y={x}^{4}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C{x}^{2}+D"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50146" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation ${x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+1=0$ for $x>0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Rearranging and Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,1$ for $x>0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/c837c3b617fa49f3d081d961196a954fada99b8d7cd12b7d7f729232e16be066.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-50197" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50197" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/18a0a935932bbe409ceb7e36459a2091ee46b74829c873bfc048a71f543d8eff.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/1cf05351f0353e95dbdff8f620f6e920650d505be88edb3e61486676cb59357c.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/3670e1b40ce25af5974059a86c502cfb68f80e81746cbb162805ab7ae4a6bce2.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/7d23f940448475b1da1008ab1d3270236abec662208e81bd0de9355e85103a38.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/90beec07c4d15fa823aee98c8a1a1e6c58846bb9b713b84848e010cc98cb3ca3.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50197" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/90beec07c4d15fa823aee98c8a1a1e6c58846bb9b713b84848e010cc98cb3ca3.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4{e}^{2x}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-4\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4(\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/cc2ee25a85be3ffdb055853f7665bd53d34003a74b96a14bb947bed39b18e83f.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-119139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/0e2d84423e017f6d126ef6b997a50d62a7de30f91c24aa64f2525ce4ae33cdd3.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/146aa5565c845f3fbfa66e6c215224236869199844cdbe51f2671c781b1c3705.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/3e93190f38d95bd30749fbd1342812c93f593a1d78243f810a3822d5d30eff82.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/4acfee397d2c301aa7d005c8467319969bdfe1a487c284e51024a1851ef8a2e3.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/557708220ba3876b0ae9dbf1d265d11e8d98cf1102ad084d93419543ede35c4b.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/146aa5565c845f3fbfa66e6c215224236869199844cdbe51f2671c781b1c3705.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-49947" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1$ for $x>0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-49947" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Rearranging and Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C,\\,x>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/8e047c3c27a000af943f50499f8c7559acceeb78cc006e796c7d353729991517.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-49947" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-49947" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-49947" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/4a2aefaff6332175608a37f6532bafd5be4ccb60a2aad8e4400a0f5767c4588a.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/5c933988eb335b7310387cfc532a6e144de3e43bfebde4c29d1e5fe76fa35027.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/763db9d469cdd9047ec823966fc922726c97cb22e6cd848a432f26bc5e6529d6.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/8910d0342d03d546117091ccd19378905b8cfc3644997cfe3ca7d95a3b4e7a6f.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/aae99f368b61351b9163646b70ea0b085019d6935334422ccb398958a81d1e47.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-49947" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/5c933988eb335b7310387cfc532a6e144de3e43bfebde4c29d1e5fe76fa35027.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{3(x-1)^{2}}{4}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{3(x-1)^{2}}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\int (x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}(\\frac{(x-1)^{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{(x-1)^{3}}{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/e0ff2e64925dcd8bdf298c47815f6e2982fe6091e1ff5dea042f585c67ef1721.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-119142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/0d14e369d621a6c2d06b4db1485ff43f6af4be2014e9d26564c9ca11e9bd38cd.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/3e475d534a8f090caa9611d865e70a9717969ddc541c55d98200e19031bffe84.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/95b3d8fc43562341f93a2bccbcbe36d2a070a2dd6687606175ab5e9580f86e2f.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/a65cbd746c3bb9abe495af168fd7c63e83ecf3d942c5fb478f3d7d312d140b4d.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/d5f4f2b65878b9c152b5c87e1fac0473f0e76455fc5762ba10f21555d68a60c4.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/3e475d534a8f090caa9611d865e70a9717969ddc541c55d98200e19031bffe84.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50196" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-3(x+1)^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50196" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-3\\int (x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-3\\int (x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(x+1)^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/03a5bf5134dc7d551b2602145c4c25081a2ad274f02c95845e5789b288e618a1.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50196" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-50196" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50196" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/1e746142e1dc26c247a6ac985c65072445658ad1f9b5ae298d246c1d81ab96bb.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/1fd9c2f2358171f102969930fde05347f50bd497f725fdc4c24fec97490f15ad.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/4bcb4f24caba3010cb8bfffecacbd392ad5951d4e42873d467c9007ad2b7ea46.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/566935c224696f817a798a9e0f608ba384b5da6af1f0bfec6ad769e910f1230c.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/83c166a9882661ec123b3f14bf76c9c7585052d0e85e24c4e41b7bbde4de9326.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-50196" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/83c166a9882661ec123b3f14bf76c9c7585052d0e85e24c4e41b7bbde4de9326.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}-2x={e}^{x/2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x+{e}^{x/2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+{e}^{x/2})\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {e}^{x/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2{e}^{x/2}+C \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+2{e}^{x/2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y={x}^{2}+2{e}^{x/2}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(0)=2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & ={0}^{2}+2{e}^{0}+C \\\\ 2 & =0+2(1)+C \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}+2{e}^{x/2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-119083" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119083" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=2x+{e}^{x/2}+1"] ["math" "y=x-\\frac{{e}^{x/2}}{2}+\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "y={x}^{2}+2{e}^{x/2}"] ["math" "y={x}^{2}+2{e}^{x/2}+2"] ["math" "y={x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{x/2}}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119083" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={x}^{2}+2{e}^{x/2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-352068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{x+1}\\,{y}^{′}=4$ that satisfies the condition $y(3)=10.$\n\n$y=\\,${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-352068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =4\\int (x+1)^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4(2(x+1)^{1/2})+C \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{x+1}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=8\\sqrt{x+1}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(3)=10$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =8\\sqrt{3+1}+C \\\\ 10 & =8(2)+C \\\\ C & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=8\\sqrt{x+1}-6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-352068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-352068" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-352068" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8\\sqrt{x+1}-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-8311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4=0$ given that $y(-1)=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-8311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-4x+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-4x+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(-1)=4$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =-4\\cdot (-1)+C \\\\ 4 & =4+C \\\\ 0 & =C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=-4x\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-8311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-8311" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-8311" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-2x-2"] ["math" "y=-4"] ["math" "y=-4x"] ["math" "y=4"] ["math" "y=4{x}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-8311" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-4x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ that satisfies the condition $f(0)=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =-2\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0)=-1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+C \\\\ -1 & =-2(0)+C \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-119045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1"] ["math" "f(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1"] ["math" "f(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3"] ["math" "f(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3"] ["math" "f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)-4x=1$ that satisfies the condition $f(1)=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=4x+1.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})+x+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+x+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(1)=-1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =2(1)^{2}+1+C \\\\ -1 & =2+1+C \\\\ C & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=2{x}^{2}+x-4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4"} {"question" "q-119046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x)=2{x}^{2}+3x-6"] ["math" "f(x)=2{x}^{2}+x-1"] ["math" "f(x)=2{x}^{2}+x-4"] ["math" "f(x)={x}^{2}+2x-4"] ["math" "f(x)={x}^{2}-2x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "q-119046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=2{x}^{2}+x-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf8cf88632a9c5ad74cf8897a740692aa2381666de5c0f8e315ed6b3974fb887"} {"question" "e-528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $f'(x) - 3\\sin(2x) = 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/example-528.json" "file_sha256" "3a32590f00e2c420f013da8f3a4737a8b530181d2ef9d897f50ac11c68eb5370"} {"question" "e-528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\nf'(x) = 3\\sin{2x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =3\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/example-528.json" "file_sha256" "3a32590f00e2c420f013da8f3a4737a8b530181d2ef9d897f50ac11c68eb5370"} {"question" "e-529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d^2 y}{\\textrm d x^2} = x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/example-529.json" "file_sha256" "e0189347ff677cac5ac0cfa1cd65796536d6ac8e035e18481ce2442d9eb3e72f"} {"question" "e-529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+C)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{3}+Cx+D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$ We cannot combine them, because $C$ is being multiplied by $x$ while $D$ is not." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/example-529.json" "file_sha256" "e0189347ff677cac5ac0cfa1cd65796536d6ac8e035e18481ce2442d9eb3e72f"} {"question" "e-530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation $y'  = 2x,$ and sketch the solution curves of this equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/example-530.json" "file_sha256" "d05449a953918ff7698cecd441b8eb5220ee5867a5257d998d8cdfb7054d114a"} {"question" "e-530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\ny = x^2+C.\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/e37771799ef5fadc259e6ea0073042a83e0974b5a2619d1af3e87a7467e6d780.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/example-530.json" "file_sha256" "d05449a953918ff7698cecd441b8eb5220ee5867a5257d998d8cdfb7054d114a"} {"question" "e-531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $f(0)=2.$\n\n$$\nf'(x) - \\dfrac{3}{1+x^2} = 0\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/example-531.json" "file_sha256" "5a875f1ec40961e0f37948d29a9fef85d57f5517e1aa46a89e350d8254139301"} {"question" "e-531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\nf'(x) = \\dfrac{3}{1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =3\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $f(x) = 3\\arctan{x} + C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0) = 2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+C \\\\ 2 & =3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)+C \\\\ 2 & =0+C \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is \n\n$$\nf(x)=3\\arctan x + 2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/example-531.json" "file_sha256" "5a875f1ec40961e0f37948d29a9fef85d57f5517e1aa46a89e350d8254139301"}] "usage" {"e-528" [{"kind" "presentations" "entity" 17592186283110}] "e-529" [{"kind" "presentations" "entity" 17592186283217}] "e-530" [{"kind" "presentations" "entity" 17592186283256}] "q-50196" [{"kind" "presentations" "entity" 17592186283257} {"kind" "responses" "entity" 17592186283257}] "e-531" [{"kind" "presentations" "entity" 17592186283371}] "q-50136" [{"kind" "presentations" "entity" 17592186283112} {"kind" "responses" "entity" 17592186283112}] "q-50139" [{"kind" "presentations" "entity" 17592186283241} {"kind" "responses" "entity" 17592186283241}]} "basis" 1153 "retractions" [[17592186097219 :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} + 4e^{2x} =-2x$."] [17592186097219 :question/worked-solution "Isolate the derivative: $y'=-2x-4e^{2x}$. Integrating term by term gives\n$$y=-x^2-2e^{2x}+C.$$\nDifferentiation recovers $-2x-4e^{2x}$."] [17592186097219 :question/difficulty 17592186045463] [17592186097220 :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} =-10$."] [17592186097220 :question/worked-solution "Integrate twice, introducing a constant at each integration:\n$$y'=-10x+C,\\qquad y=-5x^2+Cx+D.$$\nThe two constants cannot be combined because one multiplies $x$."] [17592186097220 :question/difficulty 17592186045465] [17592186097223 :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} =-3(x + 1)^{2}$."] [17592186097223 :question/worked-solution "Integrate $y'=-3(x+1)^2$:\n$$y=-(x+1)^3+C.$$\nThese are vertical translations of a decreasing cubic with a horizontal inflection point at $x=-1$. Select the diagram whose decreasing cubic curves flatten at $x=-1$."] [17592186097223 :question/difficulty 17592186045463] [17592186096419 :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $f'(x) - 3\\sin(2x) = 0$."] [17592186096419 :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\nf'(x) = 3\\sin{2x}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x$, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int f^{\\prime }(x)dx &= \\int 3\\sin 2xdx \\\\\nf(x) &= 3\\int \\sin 2xdx \\\\\n&=-\\frac{3}{2}\\cos 2x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096420 :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n$\\dfrac{\\textrm d^2 y}{\\textrm d x^2} = x$."] [17592186096420 :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int \\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}}dx &= \\int xdx \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{1}{2}x^{2} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int \\frac{dy}{dx}dx &= \\int (\\frac{1}{2}x^{2} + C)dx \\\\\ny &= \\frac{1}{6}x^{3} + Cx + D\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D$. We cannot combine them, because $C$ is being multiplied by $x$ while $D$ is not."] [17592186096421 :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $y' = 2x$, and sketch the solution curves of this equation."] [17592186096421 :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\ny = x^2+C\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C$. The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,1$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/3665168b0c99cbb50812c142637a625a.png)"] [17592186096422 :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $f(0)=2$.\n$f'(x) - \\dfrac{3}{1+x^2} = 0$"] [17592186096422 :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\nf'(x) = \\dfrac{3}{1+x^2}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x$, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int f^{\\prime }(x)dx &= \\int \\frac{3}{1 + x^{2}}dx \\\\\nf(x) &= 3\\int \\frac{1}{1 + x^{2}}dx \\\\\n&= 3\\arctan x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is\n\n$$\nf(x) = 3\\arctan{x} + C\n$$\n\nTo find a particular solution, we substitute the condition\n\n$$\nf(0) = 2\n$$\n\ninto our solution and obtain a value for $C$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= 3\\arctan (x) + C \\\\\n2 &= 3\\arctan (0) + C \\\\\n2 &= 0 + C \\\\\nC &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=3\\arctan x + 2\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186095672 17592186095673 17592186095674 17592186095675 17592186095676 17592186095678 17592186095679 17592186095680 17592186095681 17592186095682 17592186095696 17592186095697 17592186095698 17592186095699 17592186095700] "immutable_fields" [[17592186095671 :answer-field/correct] [17592186095671 :answer-field/id] [17592186095671 :answer-field/key] [17592186095671 :answer-field/type] [17592186095677 :answer-field/correct] [17592186095677 :answer-field/id] [17592186095677 :answer-field/key] [17592186095677 :answer-field/type] [17592186095695 :answer-field/correct] [17592186095695 :answer-field/id] [17592186095695 :answer-field/key] [17592186095695 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
